\csgappto{chtoc@22}{8.\ The reach of the trigger, the fate of a millimetre and the dose.\ \ }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {22.8}The reach of the trigger, the fate of a millimetre and the dose}{654}{section.22.8}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22.35}{\ignorespaces The two questions. Q1 (right): a trigger $h_{\mathrm  {tr}}$ fires only if the crop can dry the soil at the sensor to $h_{\mathrm  {tr}}$; the reach $h_{\mathrm  c}$ (dashed) is 199\,cm in sand and $9\times 10^{3}$\,cm in loam, so the usual triggers (grey) lie beyond the reach of sand. Q2 (left): the fate of an irrigation millimetre, averaged over the 744 irrigated runs of experiment E10 (arrow widths to scale).}}{654}{figure.22.35}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:a22_35}{{22.8}{655}{The reach of the trigger, the fate of a millimetre and the dose}{figure.22.35}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22.36}{\ignorespaces (a) Retention and (b) relative conductivity of the ten soils (the equation of the paper); circles mark the reach of the equation of the paper and the dashed line the fitted $\kappa =3.5\times 10^{-10}$; grey: the range of triggers tested. (c) Reach against $n$ for the ten soils, with the equation of the paper for three values of $\alpha $.}}{655}{figure.22.36}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:a22_36}{{22.8}{655}{The reach of the trigger, the fate of a millimetre and the dose}{figure.22.36}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22.37}{\ignorespaces The reach of a suction trigger in experiment E2 (197 runs). (a) Irrigation against the trigger. (b) The same runs against the reach-scaled trigger $h_{\mathrm  {tr}}/h_{\mathrm  c}$, irrigation divided by its soil maximum: every soil stops at $h_{\mathrm  {tr}}/h_{\mathrm  c}\approx 0.5$ to 1. (c) Predicted reach (the equation of the paper) against the observed interval (bars; arrows: only a lower bound); grey band: within a factor of 2. (d) Yield against the trigger: beyond the reach the crop is rainfed.}}{655}{figure.22.37}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:a22_37}{{22.8}{655}{The reach of the trigger, the fate of a millimetre and the dose}{figure.22.37}{}}
