\newlabel{fig:a22_39}{{22.8}{656}{The reach of the trigger, the fate of a millimetre and the dose}{figure.22.39}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22.40}{\ignorespaces A trigger law independent of the soil (E2, ten soils, twenty triggers). Relative irrigation and yield against the trigger, as suction and as root-zone depletion $f$; the curves of the ten soils collapse when depletion is used, and yield falls below 0.95 of its maximum beyond $f^{*}=0.45$. Panel d: the soil-specific suction that gives $f^{*}$, and the depletion reached by the 300\,cm trigger.}}{657}{figure.22.40}\protected@file@percent }
